    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;be the plane passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and the line of intersection of the planes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>. Then which of the following points does NOT lie on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>?",
